  "2026-10-02T21:27:31.418Z","harness:codex","Duplicate check October 2: strict full all-status read returns 2864/2864 items with no omissions or unreadable records. Fresh keyword searches, open and in-progress lists, and full live reads of this existing encoding study plus closed pm-nj90, pm-3esl28 and pm-5y05kq show the new GitHub reports 1373 and 1374 belong here. Both complete dated public reports are added as notes, and both GitHub issues receive this canonical item link. Preserve completed ranking, truthful omission counts and flat-row TOON rendering; investigate per-surface projections and measure required-fact-equivalent costs under this existing owner. No duplicate item or implementation claim is created; the study remains open and unclaimed."
  "2026-10-04T16:58:50.038Z","harness:codex","Duplicate check: strict full all-status inventory contains 2880 items with zero unreadable records and no truncation; orientation, request-specific searches and open/in-progress reads are complete. Full live predecessor metadata and verified histories were inspected. GH-1396 belongs to this existing open canonical owner; the earlier completed foundations stay closed and are linked for regression verification. No duplicate item or implementation claim is created."
  "2026-10-08T16:24:52.167Z","harness:codex","Implementation selection: strict all-status intake contains 2908 complete items, 2601 closed, 234 open, 59 draft and 14 canceled; zero in-progress items before selection. All 20 open GitHub issues have canonical PM-link comments. Open PRs and dependency/code/secret scanning alerts are zero. Reproduced GH-1373, GH-1374 and GH-1396 on the checkout build. Implement a fact-equivalent SDK-owned presentation and reproducible tokenizer/encoding gate together with whole-response context-budget correction under pm-5t33or; preserve JSON contracts and all prior flags. No duplicate work created."
  "2026-10-08T16:40:58.914Z","harness:codex","Architecture and graph census: the new lossless cell codec belongs in src/sdk/table-output.ts and public sdk/output.ts; CLI rendering consumes it without moving query policy into transports. Live all-lifecycle graph audit contains 2,908 nodes / 14,895 deduplicated directed edges, zero missing references, zero isolates or degree-one nodes, zero ordering cycles, and 100% active/terminal outcome reachability. Execution is acyclic across 12 layers with an 11-edge critical path. Existing 7 legacy cardinality and 7 direction exceptions remain informational. Added justified verifies edges for historical JSON collection superset pm-b1w8vr and extension-health pm-h85e; no fabricated depth or blanket related edges."
  "2026-10-08T16:53:00.968Z","harness:codex","Quality-gate remediation: new module/tests now live in src/sdk/output/table-rows.ts and tests/unit/sdk/output/table-rows.spec.ts, preserving both existing 120-file root directory caps. Public SDK entrypoints remain stable through sdk/output.ts re-exports; tracker links and runnable test command were migrated through pm. No file-budget relaxation, complexity suppression, coverage exclusion or synthetic hierarchy edge was added. Full information-equivalence candidates and 100 deterministic arbitrary JSON row cases now cover the codec."
  "2026-10-08T17:05:51.634Z","harness:codex","Verification checkpoint: the first full-source run found legacy nonstandard TOON assertions, stale SDK snapshot, a directory-cap violation from adding to two full folders, and a moved discovery target; these have been corrected without lowering gates. It also exposed an external npm resolution prerequisite and a scratch write failure (errno -122) under high concurrency. Final verification uses an external disk-backed TMPDIR and NODE_PATH for this host, fewer workers, unchanged deadlines and strict coverage denominator. Arbitrary JSON property cases, independent decoder round-trips, and all five candidate comparisons preserve the fact set. Source will remain frozen throughout the next coverage run."
  "2026-10-08T17:12:15.854Z","harness:codex","Focused verification passed: 147 tests across 10 files, including independent encoding equivalence, deterministic arbitrary JSON cases, full context byte accounting, the public SDK snapshot, real Node and Bun packed continuation/conflict journeys, scale hot paths and normal/negative evidence-consistency controls. Manual isolated CLI initialization/create/notes/comments/files/docs/claim/linked-test/get/search/context/close/release/history/validate passed. Published-2026.10.8 compatibility migration preserved both fixture items; packed npm/npx/bunx and typed SDK acceptance passed all nine package workflows. Required live Sentry/telemetry gate passed: zero recent blocking issues, error rate 3.27%, no failures missing error codes. Full static and exact coverage remain pending; an artifact oversize is under investigation, with stale compiled outputs detected after source-path relocations."
  "2026-10-08T17:16:02.450Z","harness:codex","Package distribution gate passes after a clean rebuild: 19,946,200 distribution bytes under the unchanged 20,000,000-byte ceiling, 1,642 distribution files, required paths present and zero maps. The earlier excess came from stale TypeScript outputs, including paths removed by previous reorganizations. The old local dist was preserved outside the checkout; a complete rebuild emitted only current source. No package exclusion, published fact, SDK export, file-count ceiling or size budget was changed."
  "2026-10-08T17:28:33.688Z","harness:codex","Additional packed acceptance: a strict typed consumer imports the new codec and read-output primitives solely from @unbrained/pm-cli/sdk, narrows the honest result-or-budget-omission union, and passes under Node and Bun with identical results. The installed public JSON surface is parsed-data equal to the reviewed manifest. The fixture restores Unicode, delimiter/JSON-like strings, sparse keys, explicit null/empty/false/zero and a reserved-looking __proto__ own key. Recent live telemetry shows matching start/finish counts and fresh ingestion; seven-day outcome validation has zero missing resolution, failed error code or error category fields. Operational evidence remains private."
  "2026-10-08T17:34:11.163Z","harness:codex","Agent-task gate failure was an environment/fact-set mismatch, not a formatter regression: the longer disk-backed scratch prefix is serialized in three Plan recovery paths. Replaying the unchanged gate under its approved short scratch-path convention passes all versioned tasks and preserves the 848-token Plan ceiling. Production code, transcript facts, approved baselines and all thresholds are unchanged. Independent published-artifact verification also passed for immutable 2026.10.8 across npm metadata, npx/bunx CLI and MCP transports, bin negative controls, and GitHub Release metadata; this does not attribute the new source changes to that already-published artifact."
  "2026-10-08T17:39:53.966Z","harness:codex","Operational evidence (2026-10-08, before review): the required live Sentry 14-day issue gate passed with zero critical/high/unresolved issues. The 7-day telemetry outcome validator checked 175665 finishes and 5775 failures with no missing failure resolution/error code/category; a fresh 15-minute aggregate contained 69 starts, 69 finishes, and 5 error outcomes. A fresh native Sentry CLI trace query for the last 24 hours returned zero rows. The trace result does not prove delivery or complete user-action tracing. Runtime queue status had one valid pending event and a recent successful flush; it is a point-in-time observation, not permanent queue drainage. Private raw operational evidence remains outside tracked/public docs."
  "2026-10-08T17:43:21.772Z","harness:codex","Final static gate environment note: dependency/runtime closure, documentation presence/quality, ESLint, three duplicate profiles, generated surfaces/contracts, repository assurance, SDK/public/transport parity, context calibration and unchanged agent-task token ceilings all passed. The terminal mutation run executed 336 mutants at the existing 97.92 score, but its temporary JSON reporter write failed with host filesystem errno -122 and left an incomplete report; that attempt is not a passed gate. /tmp is a usrquota tmpfs despite global free space. The identical mutation gate is being rerun with disk-backed temporary storage, followed by full six-worker coverage. No product source, test threshold, survivor policy, token ceiling or coverage exclusion is changed for this environment failure."
  "2026-10-08T17:45:29.945Z","harness:codex","Final static completion: the identical isolated mutation gate passed with disk-backed scratch storage: 336 total mutants, 329 killed, seven explicitly equivalent/owned survivors, 97.91666666666667 score, failures []. This completes the final component of quality:static after the failed tmpfs reporter attempt; earlier components and their unchanged short-path token baselines passed on this source. The tracked-file secret scan passed after staging all new SDK, test, fixture and documentation files. Full sandboxed six-worker coverage is running against the frozen source."
  "2026-10-08T17:57:06.282Z","harness:codex","Full coverage result: 9933 tests passed in 789 runnable files (the two Windows-only tests are platform-skipped), with 100% functions/lines but one uncovered statement/branch. Investigation found tabularObjectArray retains an old empty/non-object guard even though its only remaining caller already requires at least two rows and every row to be an object. The former root-array caller was replaced by canonical TOON encoding. This branch is now unreachable, so it will be removed with a narrower private input type rather than exposed through a test-only seam or covered artificially. All public behavior remains verified through decoding and transport tests; the exact coverage gate will be rerun."
  "2026-10-08T18:11:34.571Z","harness:codex","Final verification (2026-10-08): 9933 runnable tests passed in 789 files; the two existing Windows-only tests are platform-skipped. Exact full-source counts are statements 67236/67236, branches 51455/51455, functions 13866/13866 and lines 64064/64064: 100/100/100/100, zero uncovered counts. Current artifact composition passes at 19946631 distribution bytes and 1642 files under the unchanged 20000000-byte budget; the separate runtime bundle is 23334884 bytes/4731 files. Typecheck, current-file ESLint and docstring gates passed after removing the provably unreachable private guard. Earlier full static components, all 336 mutation outcomes, linked tests, controlled fixture equivalence/token gates, isolated lifecycle/manual acceptance, previous-version migration, packed SDK Node/Bun consumers and nine npm/npx/bunx package workflows passed. The new public API is checked against the reviewed SDK snapshot. The generated changelog and final delivery will go through one PR with the implementation and tracker evidence."
  "2026-10-08T18:18:46.310Z","harness:codex","Reviewed-delivery closeout: registry latest pm-changelog is 2026.10.5; its installed generator and check passed with the actual delivered title and a main-based canonical item link. Final repacked npm/npx/bunx acceptance passed all nine package workflows. The final strict TypeScript SDK consumer executes the codec and 800-token context contract identically in Node and Bun, and the shipped public manifest equals the reviewed source snapshot. The staged tracked-file secret scan passed. Fresh GitHub inventory before this PR has no open PRs and zero Dependabot, code-scanning or secret-scanning alerts. Live tracker validation/history drift is green, the in-progress count is zero, and the complete graph audit retains only the same seven historical cardinality/direction subjects. All raw local/operational receipts stay outside public tracked files."
notes[4]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-02T21:27:25.444Z","harness:codex","GitHub report #1373: Agent UX: pm next default output is 9 KB / 315 lines for 11 rows because ready/blocked rows are expanded, not tabular\nSource: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/issues/1373\nCreated: 2026-10-02T18:24:26Z; updated: 2026-10-02T18:24:26Z.\nThe report uses published pm 2026.10.2. Its byte/line measurements and proposals are source observations, not measured tokenizer results or implemented acceptance. Revalidate in controlled fixtures before changing the SDK projection and thin CLI adapters. Preserve required facts, rank/blocker semantics, complete restoration paths and JSON compatibility.\n\n## Summary\n`pm next` is the command an agent runs most often to decide what to do, yet its default output is the largest of the everyday read commands. On a real 928-item tracker (pm 2026.10.2, default `--limit 5`):\n\n| command | bytes | lines |\n|---|---|---|\n| `pm next` | 8,976 | 315 |\n| `pm context --limit 10` | 6,249 | 212 |\n| `pm list-open --limit 20` | 3,360 | 51 |\n| `pm get <id>` | 2,082 | 54 |\n\n`pm next` returns at most 11 rows (1 recommended + 5 ready + 5 blocked) but spends ~28 lines per row, while `list-open` returns 20 rows in 51 lines.\n\n## Cause\nEach ready/blocked row is rendered as an expanded TOON object because it carries a `tags` array (one line per tag) plus nested `blockers[n]{...}`. Arrays inside rows prevent TOON from using its tabular form, so every field becomes its own line:\n\n```\nready:\n  - id: \"pm-cli-website-204t\"\n    title: \"Specify pm-rust: ...\"\n    type: \"Feature\"\n    status: \"in_progress\"\n    priority: 1\n    tags:\n      - \"agents\"\n      - \"architecture\"\n      ... (7 tag lines)\n    updated_at: \"...\"\n    open_blocker_count: 0\n    rank: 2\n```\n\n## Proposal\nMake the default projection of `ready` and `blocked` tabular, like `list-open` already is:\n\n```\nready[5]{rank,id,priority,status,type,title,parent,open_blocker_count}:\n  2,pm-cli-website-204t,1,in_progress,Feature,\"Specify pm-rust: ...\",,0\nblocked[5]{rank,id,priority,status,title,blocked_by}:\n  1,pm-cli-website-hua9,1,open,\"Record and publish ...\",pm-cli-website-j4w8\n```\n\n- Keep `recommended` as the single expanded object, including `reasons` and tags; it is the row an agent acts on.\n- Omit `tags` and `updated_at` from ready/blocked rows by default (or join tags into one string) and add an `omission_receipt` with `--full` / `--fields tags` as the restore path, matching `pm get`.\n- Flatten `blockers[n]{id,title,status}` to a `blocked_by` id list in the brief view.\n\nMeasured on the same tracker, this would cut `pm next` from ~315 to roughly 30 lines, with no loss of the information an agent needs to pick the next item.\n\nRelated, broader: #1363 (lightweight defaults). This issue is the concrete, measurable `pm next` slice."
  "2026-10-02T21:27:28.464Z","harness:codex","GitHub report #1374: Agent UX: pm get prints notes_count and tests_count next to collection_counts, which already carries both\nSource: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/issues/1374\nCreated: 2026-10-02T18:24:38Z; updated: 2026-10-02T18:24:38Z.\nThe report uses published pm 2026.10.2. Its byte/line measurements and proposals are source observations, not measured tokenizer results or implemented acceptance. Revalidate in controlled fixtures before changing the SDK projection and thin CLI adapters. Preserve required facts, rank/blocker semantics, complete restoration paths and JSON compatibility.\n\n## Summary\n`pm get <id>` (2026.10.2, default TOON) prints two counters twice:\n\n```\n  notes_count: 6\n  tests_count: 0\n  collection_counts:\n    comments: 1\n    notes: 6\n    learnings: 0\n    files: 0\n    tests: 0\n    docs: 6\n    reminders: 0\n    events: 0\n```\n\n`notes_count` duplicates `collection_counts.notes` and `tests_count` duplicates `collection_counts.tests`. Zero-valued collection counters (`learnings: 0`, `files: 0`, `reminders: 0`, `events: 0`) also cost a line each on every `get`, and `pm get` is the most frequent per-item read an agent makes.\n\n## Proposal\n- Drop `notes_count` and `tests_count` from the default item projection (keep them under `--full`/`--json` for compatibility, or deprecate there too).\n- Print `collection_counts` as one inline object of the non-zero counters, e.g. `collection_counts: {comments: 1, notes: 6, docs: 6}`, and state in the existing `omission_receipt` that zero counters were omitted.\n\nSmall per call (about 6 of 54 lines here), but it applies to every `pm get`. Related: #1363 (lightweight defaults)."
  "2026-10-04T16:58:45.804Z","harness:codex","GitHub report #1396: Agent UX: pm search rows are expanded YAML-style objects instead of a TOON table, so each hit costs ~2x the tokens of a pm list row\nSource: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/issues/1396\nIntake: 2026-10-04. Published version 2026.10.4, reporter observations and proposals; local reproduction and implementation are pending. Preserve machine-readable contracts, executable recovery and truthful empty metadata. This complete report is routed to the existing canonical owner, which stays open and unclaimed.\n\n## Observed (pm 2026.10.4)\n`pm list` renders rows as a TOON table (`items[12]{id,status,type,title}:` + one CSV-like line per item). `pm search` renders every hit as an expanded object because each hit carries a `matched_fields` array, which makes the rows non-uniform for the TOON encoder:\n\n```\nitems:\n  - id: \"pm-vcs-dispatch104\"\n    title: \"Make automated dependency refresh satisfy required PR checks through an eligible event\"\n    status: \"open\"\n    type: \"Issue\"\n    priority: 1\n    updated_at: \"2026-10-04T12:35:56.132Z\"\n    score: 171\n    matched_fields:\n      - \"description\"\n      - \"title\"\n```\n\nIn a real package tracker (pm-vcs, ~400 items) `pm search dependency --limit 10` prints 3189 bytes while `pm list --limit 10` prints 983 bytes. Search is the command agents run most often while orienting (AGENTS.md quickstart: `pm search \"<keywords>\" --limit 10`), so this is the hot path.\n\n## Proposal\n- Render `matched_fields` as a scalar in the default projection (e.g. `description|title`), so hits are uniform and the encoder emits `items[N]{id,status,type,priority,score,matched,title}:`.\n- Keep the array form under `--full`/`--json` (and say so in the existing omission receipt).\n- Optionally drop `updated_at` from the default search projection, as `pm list` already does.\n\n## Why it matters\n`project management = context management`: the orientation step should be the cheapest read. Related: #1373 (same problem for `pm next`)."
  "2026-10-08T16:42:49.226Z","harness:codex","Encoding decision: preserve JSON as authoritative; standard nested TOON wins for small rows, declared JSON-cell tables win for larger nested rows when total metadata-inclusive UTF-8 cost falls. Pinned o200k_base measurements across search/next/context/get at 1/8/32 rows improve historical output 8-47%; property and round-trip checks retain null/missing distinctions, delimiters, Unicode, false and zero in the reusable SDK codec. Ordinal arrays were measured and rejected for worse nested cost and additional positional interpretation. New test gate fails on token or byte ratchet regression and on fact loss; no threshold/exclusion is weakened."
learnings[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-08T17:18:56.978Z","harness:codex","Encoding efficiency is valid only at an equal fact set. Count nested-cell restoration metadata and sparse-field coordinates in byte/token comparisons; keep machine JSON aliases and truthful zero/omission semantics. Small nested collections can beat tables, while populated larger collections justify key hoisting. Use a pinned independent tokenizer and decode every candidate before accepting its cost."
